// @log 3
// @log true
// @log true
// @log b
// D4140: a list spelled with a recursive alias's members unfolded is the alias's own list, at a
// binding, a parameter and a return. The push through the alias reads back through the list.
type J = null | string | J[]
const ys: (null | string | J[])[] = ["a", null]
const k: J = ys
print(k is J[])
if k is J[] {
  print(k.length)
  const s = k[0]
  if s is string { print(s) }
  print(k[1] == null)
  k.push("z")
  print(ys.length)
}
function take(x: J) { x is J[] }
function give(): J {
  const zs: (null | string | J[])[] = ["b"]
  zs
}
print(take(ys))
const g = give()
print(g is J[])
if g is J[] {
  const t = g[0]
  if t is string { print(t) }
}
